<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samuel Gottlieb Gmelin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1744–1774</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samuel Gottlieb Gmelin was a German physician and naturalist in Russian service. From 1768 he led an expedition of the St Petersburg Academy of Sciences through southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, the Caspian coast and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, describing its plants, animals and peoples. On his way back in 1774 he was seized by the Kaitag utsmi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a> and died in captivity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samuel-gottlieb-gmelin.jpg" alt="Samuel Gottlieb Gmelin" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samuel_Gottlieb_Gmelin_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
